course: dictionary
lesson: 12420
title: Darkly: gloomy, mysterious, threatening
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Darkly is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something, such as how they speak or look. It usually means in a threatening, mysterious or gloomy way. «"Someone is coming," the old man said darkly.» The word darkly tells you how he said it: in a serious, worried, scary way.
explain: Darkly can also mean with dark colours or in the dark. Look at the clues around the word. If the story is scary or gloomy, darkly probably means mysterious or threatening. If the sentence is about colour or light, it means dark.
explain: Darkly funny is a special phrase. It means funny about sad or frightening things. «The skeleton made a darkly funny joke about the graveyard.» Ask yourself: is the joke about something frightening or sad? Then it is darkly funny.
fact: Darkly means in a threatening, mysterious or gloomy way.
fact: Darkly can describe how someone speaks, looks or hints at something.
fact: «Hints darkly» means suggests danger or bad news without saying it plainly.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the Badger speaks darkly of the Wild Wood.
fact: A good check is to swap in a word like gloomily or mysteriously and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «"The door will open at midnight," the stranger said darkly.» How did the stranger speak? | *In a mysterious, gloomy way | With his mouth full of cake | Very quickly, like a race | Happily and loudly
exercise: «He hinted darkly that the sea was not safe.» What does darkly mean here? | In a clear, plain way | With a big smile | *In a warning, mysterious way | Under the bed
exercise: «The painting was darkly coloured, all deep browns and blacks.» What does darkly mean here? | *With dark colours | Very happily | Very loudly | Without any sound
test: «"Don't go near the old mill," warned Mrs Pike darkly.» What does darkly show? | Mrs Pike is very tired | *Mrs Pike is warning in a gloomy, serious way | Mrs Pike is joking and having fun | Mrs Pike is singing
test: Which phrase means funny about sad or frightening things? | darkly cold | softly green | *darkly funny | brightly funny
exam: «"You will regret this," he said darkly, and the room went very quiet.» What does darkly tell you about his words? | They were a happy, cheerful joke | They were whispered very softly | *They were a gloomy, threatening warning | They were sung like a song
